{"ts": "2026-08-04T04:32:40.626904+00:00", "level": "INFO", "logger": "rtl_debug_agent.nodes.checkpoint", "run_id": "a34fc179c001", "message": "awaiting_approval", "test": "dma.dma_multiburst_write_test", "file": "rtl/dma/tpe_dma.sv", "line": 239, "explanation": "In the ST_WR_DATA state, m_wdata is driven directly from the combinational sram_rdata port (line 231: assign m_wdata = sram_rdata;), relying on dp_ram's registered read port to hold the beat fetched during the single-cycle ST_WR_SRAM_RD state stable until the write happens. However the SRAM read enable (sram_en) is only asserted while state_q==ST_WR_SRAM_RD, a single cycle, and is de-asserted once the FSM moves to ST_WR_DATA. If the write side (m_wready) stalls (not immediately ready), the FSM remains in ST_WR_DATA for more than one cycle while sram_en is low, and depending on the dp_ram model's port behavero when not enabled, sram_rdata will not continue to hold correctly (e.g. may go to 0 due to enable-gated output register), producing an eventual all-zero payload as seen in mismatch row 16 (rtl=0x0...0, expected pattern). The minimal fix is to keep sram_en held (re-issuing the same-address read, harmless since sram_we stays 0) throughout ST_WR_DATA whenever the write beat hasn't completed yet, ensuring the registered sram_rdata continues to reflect the same row's data until the AXI write actually completes.", "confidence_score": 0.61, "confidence_label": "medium", "confidence_rationale": "model self-reported 0.35; file appeared in evidence; used graph traversal; consulted spec; read patched file directly", "patch_path": "/Users/bhavanibs/Documents/Claude/rtl_debug_agent/data/runs/a34fc179c001/patch.diff"}
